(1203625, 148084, 33542, '<td valign="top">I thank everyone for their comments. I did want to address one I got a couple of times about focus, I was using a large aperture because of the darkness and when I focused on the closest lava lamp it threw the farthest ones way out of focus. If you look you''ll see the picture is focused on the second lamp in the series. Not ideal, but it was the best I could come up with at the time. Any blur in the second lamp is just a result of the lava moving. <br/> <br/>Here''s a picture of the setup in case you''re interested:<br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=152010" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/33542/thumb/152010.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/33542/thumb/152010.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/33542/thumb/152010.jpg"/></a></td>', 'I thank everyone for their comments. I did want to address one I got a couple of times about focus, I was using a large aperture because of the darkness and when I focused on the closest lava lamp it threw the farthest ones way out of focus. If you look you''ll see the picture is focused on the second lamp in the series. Not ideal, but it was the best I could come up with at the time. Any blur in the second lamp is just a result of the lava moving.  Here''s a picture of the setup in case you''re interested:', '2005-03-02 15:27:17.000000', NULL, 0),
