(1203952, 149542, 22379, '<td valign="top">i find it interesting that a lot of people complained about the 1. dust and 2. white balance<br/> <br/>the dust was left intentionally, and the whitebalance altered to give the colouration that photos developed in the 70''s have today.<br/>Nostalgia, or something like it?</td>', 'i find it interesting that a lot of people complained about the 1. dust and 2. white balance the dust was left intentionally, and the whitebalance altered to give the colouration that photos developed in the 70''s have today.Nostalgia, or something like it?', '2005-03-02 17:58:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(1204041, 149186, 19880, '<td valign="top">I LOVE this picture!  Usually I do not favor over-unsharp-masked (forgive me if I''m wrong) pictures, this works very well stylisticly.  And the compositions is WONDERFUL.  The only thing, as has been pointed out, is the lack of an obvious correlation to the 70s.  Keep up the good work.</td>', 'I LOVE this picture!  Usually I do not favor over-unsharp-masked (forgive me if I''m wrong) pictures, this works very well stylisticly.  And the compositions is WONDERFUL.  The only thing, as has been pointed out, is the lack of an obvious correlation to the 70s.  Keep up the good work.', '2005-03-02 18:32:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(1204125, 149553, 31955, '<td valign="top">Congrats on your ribbon. Don''t know how some scored 1 and 2. I tried this after seeing this and come up with some not bad results. <br/> <br/>Thanks for inspiring<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-03-02 19:19:49.</i></td>', 'Congrats on your ribbon. Don''t know how some scored 1 and 2. I tried this after seeing this and come up with some not bad results.  Thanks for inspiring', '2005-03-02 19:17:15.000000', '2005-03-02 19:19:49.000000', 0),
(1204214, 148631, 28261, '<td valign="top">Oh c''mon people.  Who cares what year the building (or photog) was made in.  If you can''t see Pink Floyd''s ''The Wall'' in this shot you did not live in the 70''s nor did you qualify to vote in this challenge.</td>', 'Oh c''mon people.  Who cares what year the building (or photog) was made in.  If you can''t see Pink Floyd''s ''The Wall'' in this shot you did not live in the 70''s nor did you qualify to vote in this challenge.', '2005-03-02 20:02:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(1204227, 149545, 28261, '<td valign="top">GE, I loved this concept.  Wondering what a reshoot would look like.  Keep the blur and main viewpoint, but put someone in the shirt holding the steth up, just barely out of focus as if they were about to check our heartbeat....</td>', 'GE, I loved this concept.  Wondering what a reshoot would look like.  Keep the blur and main viewpoint, but put someone in the shirt holding the steth up, just barely out of focus as if they were about to check our heartbeat....', '2005-03-02 20:07:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(1204534, 149516, 17916, '<td valign="top">Thanks to all who voted for me. I''m slightly discouraged that the old "shoot any object behind a plate of glass with water drops" routine hasn''t got old for more people. Sorry to sound like a sore loser. I''m still grateful for my first ribbon.<br/> <br/>I had a few people ask about the setup. It''s on a large cyc wall, about 25ft wide, 20ft deep, 25ft high. (one of many benefits of working for a commercial photographer) Key light to left of model was a Profoto strobe in a 6ft octa softbox. Background was two more strobes with umbrillas. <br/> <br/>-Justin</td>', 'Thanks to all who voted for me. I''m slightly discouraged that the old "shoot any object behind a plate of glass with water drops" routine hasn''t got old for more people. Sorry to sound like a sore loser. I''m still grateful for my first ribbon. I had a few people ask about the setup. It''s on a large cyc wall, about 25ft wide, 20ft deep, 25ft high. (one of many benefits of working for a commercial photographer) Key light to left of model was a Profoto strobe in a 6ft octa softbox. Background was two more strobes with umbrillas.  -Justin', '2005-03-02 22:28:50.000000', NULL, 0),
