(1206347, 149553, 28930, '<td valign="top">markmyshots sayz: NO one says that about sunsets, waterfalls, birds, and portraits<br/> <br/>Um, I do. I say that all of them time. Thanks for reaffirming that I am in fact NO one though. In fact look at my work, I do not have a single picture of a:<br/> <br/>   1. Sunset<br/>   2. Waterfall(s)<br/>   3. Bird(s)<br/>   4. Portrait(s)<br/><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-03-03 19:34:20.</i></td>', 'markmyshots sayz: NO one says that about sunsets, waterfalls, birds, and portraits Um, I do. I say that all of them time. Thanks for reaffirming that I am in fact NO one though. In fact look at my work, I do not have a single picture of a:    1. Sunset   2. Waterfall(s)   3. Bird(s)   4. Portrait(s)', '2005-03-03 19:20:49.000000', '2005-03-03 19:34:20.000000', 0),
(1206414, 149516, 33473, '<td valign="top">Yeah, I agree w/erel... cool shot, but poor sport.<br/>The first place shot may be a familiar technique, but relative to the other shots in the contest, it stood out as exceptionally aesthetically pleasing, creative, clear, etc. Yes, obviously yours was up there to. For whatever reason the other shot rated slightly more favorably with the audience.<br/>Pat yourself on the back for taking a kick-butt shot that was hailed as superb by many, and, please, quit whining.</td>', 'Yeah, I agree w/erel... cool shot, but poor sport.The first place shot may be a familiar technique, but relative to the other shots in the contest, it stood out as exceptionally aesthetically pleasing, creative, clear, etc. Yes, obviously yours was up there to. For whatever reason the other shot rated slightly more favorably with the audience.Pat yourself on the back for taking a kick-butt shot that was hailed as superb by many, and, please, quit whining.', '2005-03-03 20:00:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(1206418, 149173, 20115, '<td valign="top">Thank you all for your comments--I am thrilled with my first ribbon.  Believe me I feel humbled being a member of a photography website that exhibits such amazing talents week after week.  I often feel I have learned something and then discover I have to keep learning the same thing over and over again.  It is often frustrating and sometimes I just want to stop, but DPC keeps challenging me.  Having lived during the 70s I wanted to portray something of substance that came from that period.  It was a real enlightment period--a waking up from old ways and a stumbling search for the new.  I am glad that someone who lived it ribboned--and I''m really glad it was me.  I so enjoy DPC and appreciate every week this method of creative expression--thanks again.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-03-04 17:31:26.</i></td>', 'Thank you all for your comments--I am thrilled with my first ribbon.  Believe me I feel humbled being a member of a photography website that exhibits such amazing talents week after week.  I often feel I have learned something and then discover I have to keep learning the same thing over and over again.  It is often frustrating and sometimes I just want to stop, but DPC keeps challenging me.  Having lived during the 70s I wanted to portray something of substance that came from that period.  It was a real enlightment period--a waking up from old ways and a stumbling search for the new.  I am glad that someone who lived it ribboned--and I''m really glad it was me.  I so enjoy DPC and appreciate every week this method of creative expression--thanks again.', '2005-03-03 20:04:44.000000', '2005-03-04 17:31:26.000000', 0),
(1206768, 149553, 34171, '<td valign="top">OUTSTANDING!!!!!!!</td>', 'OUTSTANDING!!!!!!!', '2005-03-03 23:06:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(1206784, 149553, 3569, '<td valign="top">I knew this was the one that would win.  Some commenters are wrong, peace signs were more 70s than 60s, and really it was the victory sign of WWII.  Rainbows were created by God around the beginning of Earth.   Even though the idea isn''t new, I think the shot is very creative and should have won, as it did.  Nice job.  Van</td>', 'I knew this was the one that would win.  Some commenters are wrong, peace signs were more 70s than 60s, and really it was the victory sign of WWII.  Rainbows were created by God around the beginning of Earth.   Even though the idea isn''t new, I think the shot is very creative and should have won, as it did.  Nice job.  Van', '2005-03-03 23:11:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(1206834, 149553, 24494, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by macronaut:</b></div><hr/><i> markmyshots sayz: NO one says that about sunsets, waterfalls, birds, and portraits<br/> <br/>Um, I do. I say that all of them time. Thanks for reaffirming that I am in fact NO one though. In fact look at my work, I do not have a single picture of a:<br/> <br/>   1. Sunset<br/>   2. Waterfall(s)<br/>   3. Bird(s)<br/>   4. Portrait(s) </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>yeah and for some reason you can''t make it out of the 4''s so why don''t you leave spurs alone with his blue ribbon. Great shot spurs</td>', 'Originally posted by macronaut: markmyshots sayz: NO one says that about sunsets, waterfalls, birds, and portraits Um, I do. I say that all of them time. Thanks for reaffirming that I am in fact NO one though. In fact look at my work, I do not have a single picture of a:    1. Sunset   2. Waterfall(s)   3. Bird(s)   4. Portrait(s)   yeah and for some reason you can''t make it out of the 4''s so why don''t you leave spurs alone with his blue ribbon. Great shot spurs', '2005-03-03 23:26:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(1207042, 149553, 28930, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by mrsamsa:</b></div><hr/><i>yeah and for some reason you can''t make it out of the 4''s so why don''t you leave spurs alone with his blue ribbon. Great shot spurs </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Yea, that is precisely the point. God forbid you try anything original here. Sadly, most real art will be original and not readily understood by their peers. The judging here is for people that want to take a cute picture of their cat or something - not for originality. <br/> <br/>Honestly, I am glad I am rated low. It shows that most people here don''t have a clue. Which reality has taught me that most people in-fact don''t much have. So I must be do something right. <br/> <br/>Go be a cow, follow the *&amp;^^#$ herd. Go take the 6,342,953,567 picture of Half Dome, what''s the damn point? I will continue to innovate and explore new territory. Thats where its at for me. I am currently working at 8:1 with polarized light. How many people are doing that that you know of? <br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-03-04 02:35:21.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by mrsamsa:yeah and for some reason you can''t make it out of the 4''s so why don''t you leave spurs alone with his blue ribbon. Great shot spurs   Yea, that is precisely the point. God forbid you try anything original here. Sadly, most real art will be original and not readily understood by their peers. The judging here is for people that want to take a cute picture of their cat or something - not for originality.  Honestly, I am glad I am rated low. It shows that most people here don''t have a clue. Which reality has taught me that most people in-fact don''t much have. So I must be do something right.  Go be a cow, follow the *&^^#$ herd. Go take the 6,342,953,567 picture of Half Dome, what''s the damn point? I will continue to innovate and explore new territory. Thats where its at for me. I am currently working at 8:1 with polarized light. How many people are doing that that you know of? ', '2005-03-04 02:29:58.000000', '2005-03-04 02:35:21.000000', 0),
